{
  "$comment": "PR 17 — the Lighthouse speed budget (Blueprint V2.1 speed targets) and the one list of pages it measures; the device gate (tools/device-gate.mjs) opens the same pages. CN-023 (24 Oct): the list without a database (the web job) and the list on the sample data (lighthouserc.seeded.json, follow-up 23, PR 82: products make fonts and fits cost more) are one list now, measured once, on the throwaway database holding the sample catalogue, rules and combos (never the owner's data), first visits only (no Bengali-font cookie). CI never reads this file with lhci directly: tools/lh-pages.mjs picks the pages of one run (`plan`: on a pull request the core set plus the pages its diff touches; the full set on every push to main, nightly and by hand) and writes each parallel shard's config from this one (`ci.settings` and `ci.assert` copied as they are). The app is started by CI on 127.0.0.1:3000. Pages by PR: 49 the product page (a polo with five colours) in both languages; 50/51 the T2 and T3 templates; 88 T3 in Bengali (follow-up 156); 73 the search results; 91–103 the combo page in both languages and the sets landing page; 136 the invoice; 12 and 140 the admin shell and orders; 98, 100 the set builder (the page while it is off, and the test server's preview `?try=1` of the sample Any polos rule, EXTAS_SHOP_TEST_PAGES=1, in both languages); 44 the home page with the flash sale running (the test server's trial `?try=flash`, EXTAS_SHOP_TEST_PAGES=1: the sample compare-at products, the clock at 04:12:38) in both languages; 572 a rule's own page (the sample polo pairs, template L1) in both languages.",
  "plan": {
    "$comment": "tools/lh-pages.mjs. `core`: measured on every pull request (home, a category, a product, a combo, the bag, the checkout, in English and Bengali; paths of ci.collect.url). `shardSize`: pages per runner (3 runs each); more pages than shardSize × maxShards share the shards. `fullSetWhen`: a change to a file matching one of these (repository paths, regular expressions) measures the full set, because it can change every page.",
    "core": [
      "/",
      "/bn",
      "/collections/polos",
      "/bn/collections/polos",
      "/p/essential-pique-polo",
      "/bn/p/essential-pique-polo",
      "/combo/sample-polo-chino-set",
      "/bn/combo/sample-polo-chino-set",
      "/bag",
      "/bn/bag",
      "/checkout",
      "/bn/checkout"
    ],
    "shardSize": 6,
    "maxShards": 10,
    "fullSetWhen": [
      "^pnpm-lock\\.yaml$",
      "^package\\.json$",
      "^pnpm-workspace\\.yaml$",
      "^\\.npmrc$",
      "^\\.dockerignore$",
      "^apps/web/Dockerfile$",
      "^apps/web/package\\.json$",
      "^apps/web/(next|postcss|tailwind)\\.config\\.",
      "^apps/web/tsconfig\\.json$",
      "^apps/web/src/(proxy|middleware|instrumentation)",
      "^apps/web/src/fonts/",
      "^apps/web/public/",
      "^docs/qa/page-weight\\.json$",
      "^tools/(lh-pages|page-weight|compile-hints|make-status)\\.mjs$",
      "^\\.github/workflows/ci\\.yml$",
      "^\\.github/actions/"
    ]
  },
